sentences.t:
Δύσπαρι εἶδος ἄριστε γυναιμανὲς ἠπεροπευτὰ
ποῦ τοι Δηΐφοβός τε βίη θ’ Ἑλένοιο ἄνακτος
Ἀσιάδης τ’ Ἀδάμας ἠδ’ Ἄσιος Ὑρτάκου υἱός;

sentences.l:
“Hector, since your heart is to blame the blameless,
at some other time indeed more I am set to hold back from war,
since not even me at all without might did my mother bear;

For from the time when by the ships you roused the battle of companions,
from then, being here, we are mingling with the Danaans
unceasingly;

The two alone, Deiphobus and the might of lord Helenus,
have gone, struck with long spears,
both, in the hand;

and with wondrous uproar it mingles with the sea, and in it many
waves, seething, of the much-roaring sea,
arched, white-flecked, some in front, but others upon others;

and among them you will be slain, if you bring yourself
to await my long spear, which your lily-like skin
will tear;
